{"record_id":"D08-B88-R02","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B88","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Performance Testing","example_title":"Repeated Measurement With Statistics","code":"import statistics\nfrom time import perf_counter\n\ndef measure(values: list[int], repetitions: int = 10) -> tuple[float, float]:\n    samples: list[float] = []\n    for _ in range(repetitions):\n        start = perf_counter()\n        sum(values)\n        samples.append(perf_counter() - start)\n    return statistics.mean(samples), statistics.median(samples)\n\nmean_time, median_time = measure(list(range(1000)))\nassert mean_time >= 0.0\nassert median_time >= 0.0\n","expected_behavior":"The example records multiple timing samples and calculates mean and median rather than treating one measurement as representative.","why_valid":"Repeated samples expose some measurement variability and provide basic descriptive statistics.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","At least one repetition"],"edge_cases":["Zero repetitions","System load","Garbage collection effects","Very small workloads"],"security_implications":"No direct security impact.","performance_characteristics":"Measurement cost scales with repetitions; results remain environment-dependent.","testing_method":"Run under controlled workload and environment, then compare distributions rather than isolated values.","verification_method":"Actual execution is required for timing data; no benchmark result is claimed.","version_notes":"Uses statistics.mean/median and time.perf_counter.","relationships":["D08-B21-R02","D08-B70-R04","D08-B88-R01"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Python 3.11 Documentation","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/statistics.html","version":"3.11","section":"statistics.mean and statistics.median","retrieval_date":"2026-09-16","relevance":"Statistical API seman