{"record_id":"D08-B90-R02","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B90","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Integrated Verification","example_title":"Validate Parse Persist And Read Back","code":"import sqlite3\n\ndef save_name(connection: sqlite3.Connection, user_id: str, name: str) -> None:\n    if not user_id or not name:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing required value\")\n    connection.execute(\n        \"INSERT INTO users (id, name) VALUES (?, ?)\",\n        (user_id, name),\n    )\n    connection.commit()\n\ndef test_persistence_flow() -> None:\n    connection = sqlite3.connect(\":memory:\")\n    try:\n        connection.execute(\"CREATE TABLE users (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL)\")\n        save_name(connection, \"u1\", \"Alice\")\n        row = connection.execute(\"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE id = ?\", (\"u1\",)).fetchone()\n        assert row == (\"u1\", \"Alice\")\n    finally:\n        connection.close()\n","expected_behavior":"Validated data is parameterized into SQLite, committed, and read back with the expected values.","why_valid":"The flow combines input validation, parameterized persistence, explicit commit, and verification of stored state.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","SQLite available"],"edge_cases":["Duplicate ID","Database failure","Transaction rollback","Invalid input"],"security_implications":"Parameterized SQL separates values from SQL syntax; authentication and authorization are outside this persistence example.","performance_characteristics":"Includes database I/O; no benchmark is claimed.","testing_method":"Run the complete in-memory persistence flow and assert read-back equality.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses sqlite3 standard-library APIs.","relationships":["D08-B19-R01","D08-B85-R03","D08-B89-R03"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Pyt