{"record_id":"D08-B92-R03","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B92","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Concurrency Testing","example_title":"Bounded Worker Queue Test","code":"import queue\nfrom threading import Thread\n\n\ndef test_bounded_queue() -> None:\n    work: queue.Queue[int] = queue.Queue(maxsize=2)\n    results: list[int] = []\n\n    def worker() -> None:\n        while True:\n            item = work.get()\n            try:\n                if item == -1:\n                    return\n                results.append(item * 2)\n            finally:\n                work.task_done()\n\n    thread = Thread(target=worker)\n    thread.start()\n    work.put(2)\n    work.put(3)\n    work.put(-1)\n    work.join()\n    thread.join()\n    assert results == [4, 6]\n","expected_behavior":"The worker processes queued work and signals completion for every queue item, including the termination marker.","why_valid":"Queue task accounting provides an explicit completion boundary for the producer and worker.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","Worker starts successfully"],"edge_cases":["Worker exception","Queue full","Shutdown before work completion"],"security_implications":"Bounded queues can limit resource pressure; production systems need explicit overload and shutdown policies.","performance_characteristics":"Queue operations are synchronized and incur thread coordination overhead.","testing_method":"Submit multiple work items and a termination marker, wait for queue completion, and verify results.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses queue.Queue and threading.Thread.","relationships":["D08-B37-R01","D08-B77-R04","D08-B78-R03"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Python 3.11 Documentation","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/queue.html","version":"3.