{"record_id":"D08-B92-R05","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B92","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Concurrency Testing","example_title":"Semaphore Concurrency Boundary","code":"import asyncio\n\nasync def test_semaphore_boundary() -> None:\n    semaphore = asyncio.Semaphore(2)\n    active = 0\n    peak = 0\n\n    async def task() -> None:\n        nonlocal active, peak\n        async with semaphore:\n            active += 1\n            peak = max(peak, active)\n            await asyncio.sleep(0)\n            active -= 1\n\n    await asyncio.gather(*(task() for _ in range(8)))\n    assert peak <= 2\n\n# Execute test_semaphore_boundary() with an asyncio runner.","expected_behavior":"At most two tasks hold the semaphore-protected section simultaneously.","why_valid":"The semaphore provides an explicit concurrency bound that the test measures as an invariant.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","Async event loop available"],"edge_cases":["Task cancellation","Semaphore acquisition failure","Incorrect release"],"security_implications":"Concurrency bounds can limit resource exhaustion but must be combined with queue limits, timeouts, and failure handling where appropriate.","performance_characteristics":"Concurrency is bounded at two for the protected region.","testing_method":"Run more tasks than the permitted concurrency and assert the observed peak does not exceed the bound.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses asyncio.Semaphore.","relationships":["D08-B18-R05","D08-B37-R05","D08-B77-R04"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Python 3.11 Documentation","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/asyncio-sync.html","version":"3.11","section":"Semaphore","retrieval_date":"2026-09-16","relevance":"Direct semaphore semantics."},"verification_status":"NOT_EXEC