{"record_id":"D08-B97-R04","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B97","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Deployment Verification","example_title":"Atomic Local State Replacement","code":"from pathlib import Path\nfrom tempfile import NamedTemporaryFile\nimport os\n\ndef atomic_replace(target: Path, content: str) -> None:\n    with NamedTemporaryFile(\"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\", dir=target.parent, delete=False) as temporary:\n        temporary.write(content)\n        temporary.flush()\n        os.fsync(temporary.fileno())\n        temporary_name = temporary.name\n    os.replace(temporary_name, target)\n\ndef test_atomic_replace(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    target = tmp_path / \"state.txt\"\n    atomic_replace(target, \"ready\")\n    assert target.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") == \"ready\"\n","expected_behavior":"Content is written to a temporary file in the target directory and then replaced into the target path.","why_valid":"os.replace provides an atomic replacement operation where supported by the target filesystem semantics.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","Target directory exists and permits file creation/replacement"],"edge_cases":["Crash before replacement","Filesystem semantics","Permission failure","Disk-full condition"],"security_implications":"Atomic replacement reduces partially written-file states but does not provide encryption or access control.","performance_characteristics":"Includes file write, flush, fsync, and rename/replace costs.","testing_method":"Test successful replacement and failure scenarios under the deployment filesystem.","verification_method":"Runtime execution on the target filesystem is required; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"The tmp_path parameter shown assumes a test framework fixture; the production function uses standard-library APIs.","relationships":["D08-B47-R07","D08-B85-R01","D08-B98-R02"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source"