{"record_id":"D08-B98-R03","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B98","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Production Diagnostics","example_title":"Structured Failure Classification","code":"from enum import Enum\n\nclass FailureClass(Enum):\n    RETRYABLE = \"retryable\"\n    PERMANENT = \"permanent\"\n    UNKNOWN = \"unknown\"\n\ndef classify(error: Exception) -> FailureClass:\n    if isinstance(error, TimeoutError):\n        return FailureClass.RETRYABLE\n    if isinstance(error, ValueError):\n        return FailureClass.PERMANENT\n    return FailureClass.UNKNOWN\n\ndef test_failure_classification() -> None:\n    assert classify(TimeoutError()) is FailureClass.RETRYABLE\n    assert classify(ValueError()) is FailureClass.PERMANENT\n    assert classify(RuntimeError()) is FailureClass.UNKNOWN\n","expected_behavior":"Known exception categories receive explicit classifications while unknown failures remain UNKNOWN.","why_valid":"The example avoids treating every failure as retryable or permanent without evidence.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","Classification policy is documented"],"edge_cases":["Nested exceptions","Provider-specific exceptions","Unknown failure types"],"security_implications":"Incorrect retry classification can amplify outages or duplicate sensitive operations; unknown cases should not automatically be retried.","performance_characteristics":"O(1) type checks.","testing_method":"Test each known class and an unknown exception class.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses Enum and isinstance.","relationships":["D08-B16-R03","D08-B77-R01","D08-B100-R05"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Python 3.11 Documentation","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/enum.html","version":"3.11","section":"Enum","retrieval_date":"2026-09-16","relevance