{"record_id":"D08-B98-R04","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B98","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Production Diagnostics","example_title":"Bounded Diagnostic Collection","code":"from collections import deque\n\nclass DiagnosticBuffer:\n    def __init__(self, maximum: int = 100) -> None:\n        if maximum <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"maximum must be positive\")\n        self.events: deque[str] = deque(maxlen=maximum)\n\n    def add(self, event: str) -> None:\n        self.events.append(event)\n\ndef test_diagnostic_bound() -> None:\n    buffer = DiagnosticBuffer(2)\n    buffer.add(\"a\")\n    buffer.add(\"b\")\n    buffer.add(\"c\")\n    assert list(buffer.events) == [\"b\", \"c\"]\n","expected_behavior":"The diagnostic buffer retains at most its configured number of recent events.","why_valid":"deque(maxlen=...) provides explicit bounded storage rather than unbounded diagnostic accumulation.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","Positive maximum size"],"edge_cases":["Maximum of one","Very large maximum","Sensitive diagnostic content"],"security_implications":"Bounded diagnostics reduce memory growth but retained logs may still contain sensitive information and require appropriate handling.","performance_characteristics":"Append is O(1); memory is bounded by maxlen.","testing_method":"Insert more events than the configured capacity and verify eviction behavior.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses collections.deque with maxlen.","relationships":["D08-B13-R03","D08-B48-R03","D08-B93-R02"],"provenance":{"source_type":"official_documentation","source":"Python documentation","title":"Python 3.11 Documentation","publisher":"Python Software Foundation","url":"https://docs.python.org/3.11/library/collections.html","version":"3.11","section":"deque","retrieval_date":"2026-09-16","relevance":"Direct deque maxlen semantics."},"verification_status":