{"record_id":"D08-B99-R01","dataset_id":"D08","batch_id":"B99","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"End-To-End Reference Implementation","example_title":"Validate Authorize Execute Verify","code":"from dataclasses import dataclass\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass Command:\n    actor: str\n    action: str\n\nclass System:\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self.state = \"idle\"\n\n    def execute(self, command: Command) -> str:\n        if command.actor != \"operator\":\n            raise PermissionError(\"unauthorized\")\n        if self.state != \"idle\":\n            raise RuntimeError(\"invalid state\")\n        self.state = command.action\n        return self.state\n\n    def verify(self, expected: str) -> bool:\n        return self.state == expected\n\ndef test_end_to_end() -> None:\n    system = System()\n    command = Command(\"operator\", \"active\")\n    result = system.execute(command)\n    assert result == \"active\"\n    assert system.verify(\"active\")\n","expected_behavior":"The example validates actor authorization and state preconditions, executes the action, then verifies observed state against the expected result.","why_valid":"The lifecycle separates request, authorization, execution, and outcome verification.","preconditions":["Python 3.11+","The simplified actor and state policy is explicitly defined"],"edge_cases":["Unauthorized actor","Invalid state","Execution failure","Verification mismatch"],"security_implications":"Production systems require authenticated identity, scoped policy, durable audit, concurrency control, and authoritative verification.","performance_characteristics":"O(1) for the in-memory operations shown.","testing_method":"Test authorized success and each failure boundary.","verification_method":"Runtime execution; not performed during dataset generation.","version_notes":"Uses dataclass and explicit state transitions.","relationships":["D08-B90-R01","D08-B90-R05","D