{"record_id":"D09-B60-R01","dataset_id":"D09","batch_id":"B60","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Integrated Resilience","example_title":"Retry Loop Without Backoff","invalid_code":"for _ in range(100):\n    try:\n        return service.call()\n    except TimeoutError:\n        continue","failure_type":"retry_storm","expected_error":"No mandatory Python exception; repeated immediate retries can amplify load against an already degraded dependency.","why_it_fails":"The retry mechanism has no delay, jitter, concurrency budget, or failure classification.","diagnostic_evidence":["100 retries are attempted immediately","TimeoutError alone controls retry","no backoff exists"],"likely_cause":"Treating retries as a free reliability mechanism.","corrected_code":"import time\n\nfor attempt in range(5):\n    try:\n        return service.call()\n    except TimeoutError:\n        if attempt == 4:\n            raise\n        time.sleep(0.5 * (2 ** attempt))","preconditions":["TimeoutError represents a retryable transient condition and the delay policy is acceptable."],"edge_cases":["service recovery","persistent outage","many concurrent callers","request deadline"],"security_implications":"Retry storms can become an availability vulnerability and amplify denial-of-service conditions.","performance_characteristics":"Backoff increases worst-case latency while reducing immediate retry pressure.","testing_method":"Simulate dependency outage under concurrent clients and measure request/retry volume.","verification_method":"Verify retry count, delay, jitter policy, deadline, and failure classification.","version_notes":"Python 3.11+ time.sleep behavior; production async systems should use non-blocking delay where appropriate.","relationships":[{"type":"related_to_dataset","target_dataset":"D22","target_scope":"reliability"},{"type":"related_to_dataset","target_dataset":"D39","target_scope":"performance diagnosis"},{"type":"related_to