{"record_id":"D09-B60-R04","dataset_id":"D09","batch_id":"B60","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Integrated Resilience","example_title":"Circuit Breaker Opens Without Half-Open Recovery Probe","invalid_code":"circuit_open = False\n\nif circuit_open:\n    raise RuntimeError('unavailable')\ntry:\n    service.call()\nexcept TimeoutError:\n    circuit_open = True","failure_type":"irreversible_circuit_state","expected_error":"No mandatory Python exception beyond the first failure; once open, the example contains no mechanism to test recovery and close the circuit.","why_it_fails":"The state machine has an open transition but no cooldown, half-open probe, or recovery transition.","diagnostic_evidence":["circuit_open becomes True on failure","no code resets circuit_open","future calls always fail once open"],"likely_cause":"Implementing failure blocking without modeling recovery.","corrected_code":"import time\n\nopened_at = None\ncooldown = 30\n\ndef call():\n    global opened_at\n    if opened_at is not None and time.monotonic() - opened_at < cooldown:\n        raise RuntimeError('circuit open')\n    try:\n        result = service.call()\n    except TimeoutError:\n        opened_at = time.monotonic()\n        raise\n    else:\n        opened_at = None\n        return result","preconditions":["A single-process simplified circuit state is sufficient for this example."],"edge_cases":["concurrent probes","distributed circuit state","clock changes","partial recovery"],"security_implications":"A permanently open protection or monitoring dependency can create an availability gap that remains undetected.","performance_characteristics":"Circuit state checks are O(1); recovery policy controls probe frequency.","testing_method":"Simulate failure, cooldown, successful recovery, and repeated failure.","verification_method":"The resilience state machine must contain tested failure and recovery transitions.","version_notes":"Python