{"record_id":"D09-B60-R05","dataset_id":"D09","batch_id":"B60","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":"3.11+","topic":"Integrated Resilience","example_title":"Graceful Shutdown Stops New Work but Leaves Active Work Unverified","invalid_code":"shutting_down = True\n\nexecutor.shutdown(wait=False)\nprint('shutdown complete')","failure_type":"shutdown_outcome_false_success","expected_error":"No mandatory Python exception; shutdown can be reported complete while previously submitted work is still running.","why_it_fails":"wait=False does not mean all submitted work has completed. The printed status confuses initiation of shutdown with verified completion.","diagnostic_evidence":["executor.shutdown(wait=False) returns before all work necessarily completes","shutdown complete is printed immediately","active tasks have no outcome verification"],"likely_cause":"Treating shutdown request acceptance as shutdown completion.","corrected_code":"executor.shutdown(wait=True)\nprint('shutdown complete')","preconditions":["The application can safely wait for active tasks during shutdown."],"edge_cases":["hung task","task failure","shutdown deadline","external side effects"],"security_implications":"Reporting shutdown completion before security-sensitive work has stopped can create misleading operational state.","performance_characteristics":"wait=True increases shutdown latency until active work completes.","testing_method":"Submit controlled long-running tasks and verify completion status before reporting shutdown complete.","verification_method":"Shutdown completion must be based on the defined lifecycle condition, not merely a shutdown request.","version_notes":"Python 3.11+ concurrent.futures Executor semantics.","relationships":[{"type":"related_to_dataset","target_dataset":"D05","target_scope":"resource lifecycle"},{"type":"related_to_dataset","target_dataset":"D22","target_scope":"reliability"},{"type":"related_to_dataset","target_dataset":"D4