{"record_id":"D10-B53-R02","dataset_id":"D10","dataset_version":"0.1-draft","batch_id":"B53","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":">=3.11","topic":"Rate limiting diagnosis","error_title":"HTTP 429 retried without respecting server-provided retry guidance","failing_code":"for _ in range(10):\n    try:\n        return call_api()\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:\n        if exc.code != 429:\n            raise","error_signature":"HTTP 429 Too Many Requests","observed_failure":"The client retries immediately or on a fixed schedule without using the API's rate-limit contract.","diagnostic_evidence":["429 explicitly signals request-rate limiting.","The retry loop has no delay or Retry-After interpretation.","Immediate retries can prolong the rate-limited condition."],"candidate_causes":["Exceeded request quota","Burst traffic","Shared tenant quota","Provider-specific throttling"],"root_cause":"The retry policy ignores server-provided rate-limit semantics.","corrective_action":"Classify 429 as a throttling condition and honor documented retry timing while bounding retries.","corrected_code":"import time\n\nfor attempt in range(3):\n    try:\n        return call_api()\n    except RateLimited as exc:\n        if exc.retry_after is None:\n            delay = min(2 ** attempt, 30)\n        else:\n            delay = min(exc.retry_after, 30)\n        time.sleep(delay)\nraise RuntimeError('rate limit persisted')","expected_behavior":"The client applies bounded backoff and respects documented server retry guidance.","verification_method":"Use a fake API returning controlled rate-limit responses and verify delays and retry count.","regression_test":"Assert that 429 cannot cause an unbounded immediate retry loop.","preconditions":["API exposes rate-limit semantics through status or exception metadata"],"edge_cases":["Missing Retry-After","Very large Retry-After","Clock skew","Shared quota across processes"],"security_implications":"Rate-l