{"record_id":"D10-B58-R02","dataset_id":"D10","dataset_version":"0.1-draft","batch_id":"B58","knowledge_type":"VERIFIED_FACT","language":"Python","language_version":">=3.11","topic":"API retry diagnosis","error_title":"Retry delay resets after each application restart","failing_code":"for attempt in range(3):\n    try:\n        return call_remote()\n    except RetryableRemoteError:\n        time.sleep(2 ** attempt)","error_signature":"Coordinated retry bursts after repeated process restarts","observed_failure":"The retry schedule exists only in process memory, so repeated restarts reset the backoff state and can recreate immediate traffic bursts.","diagnostic_evidence":["Attempt count begins at zero after every process restart.","No distributed retry budget or jitter is retained.","Multiple instances can synchronize their retry schedules."],"candidate_causes":["Crash/restart loop","Orchestrator repeatedly restarts process","Fleet-wide synchronized failures","No persistent retry state"],"root_cause":"Retry control is local and deterministic while the failure occurs across a distributed population.","corrective_action":"Use bounded exponential backoff with jitter and, where appropriate, externalized operation state or queue-level retry controls.","corrected_code":"import random\nimport time\n\nfor attempt in range(3):\n    try:\n        return call_remote()\n    except RetryableRemoteError:\n        base = min(2 ** attempt, 30)\n        delay = random.uniform(0, base)\n        time.sleep(delay)\nraise RuntimeError('retry budget exhausted')","expected_behavior":"Independent clients avoid synchronized retry bursts while maintaining a bounded retry budget.","verification_method":"Simulate multiple clients experiencing the same failure and compare retry timestamps.","regression_test":"Verify delay remains bounded and includes jitter across repeated retry attempts.","preconditions":["Retryable operation with acceptable retry semantics"],"edge_cases":["Process restart","Lar